<!--
  Trim warnings of libraries that do not apply to lip, each with the reason.

  Spectre.Console.Cli reads by reflection the commands and settings of lip, which the trimmed
  lip keeps whole (TrimmerRootAssembly lip), and its own types, which it keeps whole too
  (TrimmerRootAssembly Spectre.Console.Cli). The options of lip are of types whose converters
  TypeDescriptor knows without reflection: string, string[] and bool; none is a flag value
  (FlagValue) or a dictionary (pair deconstruction), which Spectre.Console.Cli creates by
  reflection.

  Scriban awaits the values of functions by reflection when it renders a template
  asynchronously; lip renders templates synchronously (Template.Render).

  Flurl reads the properties of an object given for query parameters, headers or cookies, and
  Flurl.Http serializes an object given as JSON, by reflection. lip gives them strings only and
  sends or receives no JSON through them.
-->
